---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ExternalLink, Monitor, Terminal, BookOpen } from 'lucide-react';
---

<BaseLayout title="Tutorial - DTRules" description="Learn how to set up and use DTRules with the visual UI and CLI.">
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">
          Getting Started <span class="gradient-text">Tutorial</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Learn how to set up DTRules locally. Edit decision tables, explore entities, and run tests.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Demo Options -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <!-- Run Locally -->
        <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-8">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="p-2 bg-blue-500/10 rounded-lg">
              <Monitor className="h-6 w-6 text-blue-400" />
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Run Locally</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-6">
            The best way to experience DTRules is to run the UI locally with the Go backend.
            This gives you full access to edit and test decision tables.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-4 mb-6">
            <div class="glass rounded-lg p-4">
              <div class="text-sm font-medium mb-2">1. Start the Backend</div>
              <pre class="text-xs bg-background/50 rounded p-2 overflow-x-auto"><code>cd go
go run ./cmd/api</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="glass rounded-lg p-4">
              <div class="text-sm font-medium mb-2">2. Start the Frontend</div>
              <pre class="text-xs bg-background/50 rounded p-2 overflow-x-auto"><code>cd ui
npm install
npm run dev</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="glass rounded-lg p-4">
              <div class="text-sm font-medium mb-2">3. Open Browser</div>
              <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Navigate to <code class="text-blue-400">http://localhost:5173</code></p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <a
            href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart-ui"
            class="w-full px-6 py-3 gradient-button text-white font-semibold rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center gap-2"
          >
            <BookOpen className="h-5 w-5" />
            Full Setup Guide
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- CLI Demo -->
        <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-8">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="p-2 bg-purple-500/10 rounded-lg">
              <Terminal className="h-6 w-6 text-purple-400" />
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">CLI Demo</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-6">
            Use the Go CLI to validate and execute decision tables directly from the command line.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-4 mb-6">
            <div class="glass rounded-lg p-4">
              <div class="text-sm font-medium mb-2">Build the CLI</div>
              <pre class="text-xs bg-background/50 rounded p-2 overflow-x-auto"><code>cd go
go build -o dtrules ./cmd/dtrules</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="glass rounded-lg p-4">
              <div class="text-sm font-medium mb-2">List Decision Tables</div>
              <pre class="text-xs bg-background/50 rounded p-2 overflow-x-auto"><code>./dtrules -rules ../sampleprojects/CHIP/xml -list</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="glass rounded-lg p-4">
              <div class="text-sm font-medium mb-2">Execute with Trace</div>
              <pre class="text-xs bg-background/50 rounded p-2 overflow-x-auto"><code>./dtrules -rules ../sampleprojects/CHIP/xml \
  -entry Compute_Eligibility -trace</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>

          <a
            href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart-go"
            class="w-full px-6 py-3 border border-border hover:bg-accent/50 text-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center gap-2 transition-colors"
          >
            <BookOpen className="h-5 w-5" />
            Go Quick Start
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sample Project Info -->
      <div class="mt-16 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-center">CHIP Sample Project</h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground text-center mb-8">
            The demo uses the CHIP (Children's Health Insurance Program) sample project,
            which demonstrates real-world eligibility determination logic.
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-3xl font-bold gradient-text mb-2">7</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Decision Tables</div>
            </div>
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-3xl font-bold gradient-text mb-2">7</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Entities</div>
            </div>
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-3xl font-bold gradient-text mb-2">40+</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Business Rules</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- GitHub Link -->
      <div class="mt-12 text-center">
        <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-4">
          Want to explore the full source code?
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/dtrules/dtrules"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 border border-border hover:bg-accent/50 text-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg transition-colors"
        >
          View on GitHub
          <ExternalLink className="h-4 w-4" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
